WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.652
(Prayers). ...

00:00:00.654 --> 00:00:01.553
Hon. Yonah Martin (Acting

00:00:01.555 --> 00:00:02.488
Leader of the Opposition):

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:10.696
Honourable senators,

00:00:10.698 --> 00:00:11.630
Veterans' Week invites us to

00:00:11.632 --> 00:00:12.264
pause and look upon the

00:00:12.266 --> 00:00:13.098
fragile gift of peace with

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:13.899
profound awe and sacred

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:14.833
gratitude. We honour the more

00:00:14.835 --> 00:00:15.634
than two million Canadians who

00:00:15.636 --> 00:00:17.369
have stepped forward in uniform

00:00:17.371 --> 00:00:18.170
throughout our history,

00:00:18.172 --> 00:00:19.037
bearing the weight of our

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:20.806
highest ideals, and we grieve

00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:24.710
the precious souls who did not .

00:00:24.712 --> 00:00:25.577
Remembrance lives deeply

00:00:25.579 --> 00:00:31.717
within our own shared Canadian

00:00:31.719 --> 00:00:32.651
the memories of grandparents

00:00:32.653 --> 00:00:33.385
and loved ones who answered

00:00:33.387 --> 00:00:38.957
the call in world wars,

00:00:38.959 --> 00:00:39.791
conflicts, and peacekeeping

00:00:39.793 --> 00:00:40.726
missions across the globe. We

00:00:40.728 --> 00:00:41.460
honour the quiet dignity of

00:00:41.462 --> 00:00:43.228
those who returned home, the

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.096
steadfast hearts of those

00:00:44.098 --> 00:00:45.030
currently serving in uniform,

00:00:45.032 --> 00:00:47.799
and the hidden sacrifices of

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:48.734
military families whose lives

00:00:48.736 --> 00:00:59.545
have been forever shaped by ser.

00:00:59.547 --> 00:01:00.612
Like millions of people of

00:01:00.614 --> 00:01:01.647
Korean heritage across Canada a

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:02.548
around the world, I owe my

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:03.382
very existence and every

00:01:03.384 --> 00:01:05.951
breath of freedom I take to

00:01:05.953 --> 00:01:06.852
the veterans of the Korean War

00:01:06.854 --> 00:01:08.887
who crossed oceans to defend a

00:01:08.889 --> 00:01:09.755
land they had never known.

00:01:09.757 --> 00:01:11.590
Their selfless courage changed

00:01:11.592 --> 00:01:12.424
the course of history in

00:01:12.426 --> 00:01:18.096
profound ways.

00:01:18.098 --> 00:01:19.064
One of our most sacred duties

00:01:19.066 --> 00:01:23.602
is to pass these truths on to o

00:01:23.604 --> 00:01:24.503
children and grandchildren,

00:01:24.505 --> 00:01:25.437
ensuring they understand that

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:26.538
our peace was bought with a

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:30.909
heavy price.

00:01:30.911 --> 00:01:31.910
Tomorrow in this chamber, and

00:01:31.912 --> 00:01:37.649
wherever we gather on November

00:01:37.651 --> 00:01:38.784
11 we stand not merely to look

00:01:38.786 --> 00:01:39.785
back, but to pledge our living

00:01:39.787 --> 00:01:43.689
loyalty to their memory.

00:01:43.691 --> 00:01:44.690
When the silence falls at the

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:48.427
eleventh hour, may we hold thei

00:01:48.429 --> 00:01:49.561
courage close to our hearts,

00:01:49.563 --> 00:01:53.298
never take our freedoms for gra

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.166
and resolve to always be

00:01:54.168 --> 00:01:55.100
worthy of the sacrifices that

00:01:55.102 --> 00:02:02.374
made our lives possible.

00:02:02.376 --> 00:02:03.242
We will remember them.
